WEBVTT

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.320
On the right, a new First.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Keith!

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.030
People of the black bones,

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.320
-gather ye together at the promised land.
-Keith! Keith!

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.960
Keith Flick.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.640
Keith.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.130
Genie, no!

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.960
Don't look!
Keith.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.440
Genie!
Keith.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.000
Genie!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.340
He mutilated just her face.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:42.600
Like the cycle of death and rebirth,
it will repeat itself, continuing forever.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:44.760
Keith.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.570
I love you, Keith.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.780
I'll reconstruct it.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.580
Falling. Shaking. Falling.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.740
It'll be just like before.
Just like how she used to be.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.080
I'll put everything I have into it.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.350
A new First.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.190
Another Fourth.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.210
I guess I should go to the library.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.990
It's connected properly.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.540
Koku!

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.210
Yo!

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.550
-The Royal Library?
-Yes.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.130
What for?

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.970
To research something.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.260
Research something?
Why not just do a web search?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.260
I don't have anything
like a computer or cell phone.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.650
Oh yeah, I've never seen you use either.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.980
Well, I don't need them.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.320
Wow, really? I'd die without mine.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.280
I won't.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.570
But they're so convenient!

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.030
I'm not interested in convenience.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.610
You are strange, after all.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.790
I see. You have a cute face,
but you're still single

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:13.760
because you're nit picky-

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.080
Are you off today, Lily?
because you're nit picky-

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.080
Are you off today, Lily?

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.670
I'm off duty, so close enough.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.880
Where are you going?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.380
Running an errand.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.010
So, Koku, what's your type?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.470
The cultured type? Older girls?

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.520
How about I introduce you to my friends?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.650
Up there. Isn't that the turn?

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.850
Whoops!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.990
ROYAL LIBRARY

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.950
This is expired.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.410
Right here.
It expired on the seventh of last month.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.830
We can renew it right away.
If you have ID.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.390
This is expired, too.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.180
A year ago.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:15.100
Next person in line, please!

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.980
Do you know what "Canopus" is?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.070
A star.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.580
It's not visible at this latitude, but a
little south, it's just above the horizon.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:35.030
I asked thinking you wouldn't know.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.040
Then you've underestimated me.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.590
Do you know a lot about the stars?

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:44.130
Not at all. My sweetie in high school
was totally into that stuff.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.380
There's that museum next door
to the cathedral, right?

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.720
He droned on and on in the planetarium
there even though I'd never asked.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.600
He put me half to sleep.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.310
For some reason,
I kind of remember the star names.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.980
Good times, good times!

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.070
This "sweetie" was a boy, right?

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.490
You really do underestimate me, don't you?

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.370
This will be acceptable.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:23.790
Fill out the renewal form at window three,
down the hall to the right, and come back.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:28.970
-You said you could do it right away!
-They can, at window three.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.090
Okay, next in line!

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.590
Touch Canopus.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.980
-Are you all right, son?
-Damn it.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:29.200
Are you all right, son?

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:10.740
Hey there!

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.070
What's wrong with your leg?

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.330
-Sorry to intrude!
-Go away.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.920
-Buns!
-What are you, deaf?

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.800
I said, go away.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.510
You don't like these?

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.550
I also have a single
Zeppole di San Giuseppe!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.600
Have you ever had one?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.720
No, I haven't. So go away.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.560
I think you can probably tell,

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.520
I have no intention of backing down.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.730
I even bought buns.

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:52.650
What a day.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.380
Can I help with anything?

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:15.090
"Genie" means "Genius," right?
Who gave you that nickname?

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.750
Boris?

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:17.760
I don't know.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.660
So, about Killer B.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:49.170
Killer B, and his victims,
who are the perpetrators in these cases,

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.710
are becoming more complicated
as they're becoming more brutal.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:57.180
They all end with your standard "serial
killer rampage and self-destruction."

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:01.600
And the B mark left at the scenes
are more assertive than in the past.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:05.180
Also, did you know
that over the past few years,

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.980
gold thefts have overlapped
with visually flashy crimes?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.940
They're opportunistic crimes, and Foreign
Affairs Section Two is overseeing them.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.240
Lately, Killer B-related crimes
are happening without any fanfare.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.240
That's troubling, too, isn't it?

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.240
Is B really B?

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:25.330
It's as if there's some other meaning,
and he's asking someone else what that is.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.130
And then, originally--

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.370
Here.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:36.040
Um... This is for me?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.090
If you're not eating, leave.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.180
Thanks for the food.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.850
So eat. Then leave.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:42.850
I said I'm not leaving.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.850
Man, you're one stubborn old dude.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.360
Lily?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.210
Everything's all jumbled up
in my head now.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:15.500
Coffee?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.040
I'd love some! What kind?

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.050
My blend.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.630
Anyway, it's all tangled together.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.850
It's a bad omen. I can't shake
that feeling for some reason.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:31.310
I decided not to think,
cause everyone told me not to,

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.900
but I started thinking anyway.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:38.020
And once I did, everything got
all jumbled up inside my head.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:41.360
So, after agonizing over all this stuff
all night,

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.370
I decided to come here.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.370
That doesn't strike me as a smart move.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:52.170
"Smart doesn't mean right. Sometimes
being foolish is the right answer."

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.120
That's one of your lines, isn't it?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.130
Boris, huh? He also gave you my address?

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.510
He told me all sorts of things about you.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.850
He's an old-timer,
so he rambles on without me asking.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.970
But coming here today was my own idea.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:12.730
Tell Boris that I said
not to put dumb ideas into your head.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.500
It's a pain.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.070
I thought you could untangle them.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:22.900
I thought that only you could
untangle the knots in my head.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.860
That's why I came. Keith Flick.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:29.700
Only you, the one Boris calls Genie.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.630
Why's it doing that? What's going on?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.760
So, let's say the culprit
in these incidents is this pastry.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.130
He's one tasty-looking criminal.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.300
This red bean bun is the perp.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:47.130
The Zeppole is Killer B.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.010
We know there's no interaction
between these two.

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:52.190
So, there's a gap in these cases.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:57.770
I figure there's something in this gap
that links the two cases together.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:11:59.860
Ta-da!

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:04.070
It looks like the red bean bun,
but it's a coffee bun.

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:12.710
And we also tear the red bean bun
in half and...

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.440
It only makes sense this way.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.630
I've lost my appetite.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.880
I know, right? It's all a jumble. Chaos!

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.500
And?

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:26.670
Don't you see it?

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:29.400
This is the cases' structure!

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.600
It's a mess, you mean?

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:31.930
No!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.810
Who can understand this?

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.310
The chaos is inside your head!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.190
Straighten it out and then speak, nitwit.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.610
I can't, that's why I came here!

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.700
Then you should've said that first.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.740
And apologize to these buns
and their bakers.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.580
Playing with food...

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.120
Idiots shouldn't make
pointless presentations.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.160
I'm not--

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:02.630
My point is, there's a third player
out there no one knows about.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.380
It's disguised as something else.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.340
So, although it's in plain sight,
no one knows.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.720
A balance is being maintained,

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.140
but when its disguise fails,
it'll take action,

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.730
expand with the speed
of a subatomic particle

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.230
and swallow up the whole country.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.780
And then a cycle of one incident
after another will begin,

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.700
and before we know it,

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.070
we'll be reduced to nothing more
than helpless onlookers.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.070
I know that it sounds stupid,
like some conspiracy theory,

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.870
but I can't find anything
that disproves it.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.790
While I was thinking about it all,
my head got all jumbled up.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.710
To be perfectly honest, I'm scared now.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.560
Now you listen and listen close,
you dumb kid.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.030
Keep your nose out of this from now on.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.450
-Why should I do that?
-For your own good.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:14.870
What do you mean by that?

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:20.630
It means this isn't something some idiot
should get involved in out of curiosity.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.040
If you understand, leave.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.890
Okay, I'll be frank too.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.800
Not a chance in hell!

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:35.390
You little--

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:44.440
Okay, then.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.360
Lily!

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:55.450
Huh?

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:57.290
Boris?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.210
You two...

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.250
What kind of kinky stuff are you up to?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.340
Kaela, what do you want for dinner?

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:23.230
Huh?

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:28.530
Keith slipped and fell,
then I did when I tried to help him.

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.070
That's all.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.860
Sorry. I just assumed...

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:33.820
Why are you here?

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.910
Boris!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.790
Boris sent this.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.670
"Everybody come to Keith's place,
we're gonna do something."

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:49.330
We're having a party, right?
Mario's buying beer on his way over.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.830
I-I made a little mistake!

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:55.640
I-I have no idea
how to use these things!

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.970
You hit "group send," didn't you?

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.060
By the way, why is your door broken?

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:15.620
How is it?

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.200
It's very high purity.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.670
It seems fine. Well done.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:31.290
Where are the others?

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:34.550
They got assignments for their cover jobs.
They're out.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:35.840
From Regulus?

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:38.720
Has his mood improved?

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.760
Oh, he's rather angry.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:45.260
Because the retrieval of our quarry
is so far behind schedule.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.940
He's tougher than expected.
He's too powerful to take on alone.

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:52.230
Even someone
as skilled as Izanami was killed.

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:55.270
We should rethink our capture method.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:59.610
Shall I go to Regulus and tell him
that's your considered opinion?

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:00.900
No.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:14.330
This turned into an actual drinking party.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.590
Now, now.
Having a little fun will do you some good.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.800
This is all because of you
and your big mouth.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.340
Take responsibility.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:26.300
You mean about Lily?
She's an interesting one, don't you think?

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:28.400
I'm talking about your loose lips.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.110
We've known each other for five years now,

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:35.070
and I still can't tell
if she's smart or a fool.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.570
A fool, obviously.

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:40.530
She gets things, even when she doesn't.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.860
She's a strange girl, for sure.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.910
A wiseass who's totally direct.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.540
She's got big brown eyes,

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:51.500
is a lefty, and is a dainty little thing.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.720
Doesn't she remind you of her a little?

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:05.680
Whew, it's freezing out here!
I gotta take a leak!

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.780
Boris!

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.730
You've had enough, Kaela!

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.240
Don't be such an old man!

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.940
I'm not an old man!
Don't be such an old man!

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.480
She's nothing like her.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:01.570
Need a hand?

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.450
N-No, I'm good.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.660
I was just leaving.

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.420
Okay...

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:19.020
Bran?

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:19.920
Good night!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.840
Mind the fort!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.400
Brandon?

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.280
Oops! I forgot all about him!

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:45.580
Hello?

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.780
Where are you right now?

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:50.290
At Keith's place. Everybody's here.

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:51.710
Keith's?

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:54.210
Eric already left. Are you coming?

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.640
So did Jean! That party pooper!

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:58.420
If you're coming, grab some beer!

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.170
And snacks!

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.670
Don't forget snacks!

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:31.410
I'll be right there.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.170
What a weird kid.

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.340
Come on, hurry up, hurry up.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.980
POLLUTED AREA, NO TRESPASSING

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:23.540
Koku? Koku?
Are you okay?

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.330
You sure are sentimental.

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.040
<i> I hope we meet again!</i>

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:27.800
<i>We will!</i>

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:30.340
It's all for you.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:33.730
Touch Canopus.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:45.020
Even if I'm called a demon because of it,

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:48.070
I'll do whatever it takes.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:52.910
I'll find you.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:15.390
Someday I’ll be gone

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:23.980
To somewhere that we belong

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:29.360
And god has never played his role

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:33.660
Because I’m the one who saves my soul

00:22:34.030 --> 00:22:38.790
It is a perfect world we’re longing for

00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:41.920
So long...

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:12.570
Cursed shadows haunt and gather

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:16.200
In the city of no answer

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:20.500
as we follow endless questions

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.420
hands up in the same reflection

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:28.340
just used to be
Sometimes we try to feel how things

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:32.470
in yesterdays

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:36.550
No one ever make it better, no one ever lives forever

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:39.930
Wake me up and let me go

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:48.150
Someday I’ll be gone

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:54.240
To somewhere we all belong

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:56.990
For so long
